{"availability":"available","full":"yashdagar/datecrew-match-check","name":"datecrew-match-check","description":"Prototype for The Date Crew assessment: checks profiles against client preferences before sending and triages free-text rejections","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-06T07:50:55Z","updated":"2026-10-06T19:01:03Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://datecrew-match-check.netlify.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://datecrew-match-check.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:31.278Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:31.278Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:31.278Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T22:54:31.278Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Prototype for The Date Crew Product Engineer assessment (Part 3).","Live demo: (runs this repo's Python in the browser via Pyodide, on the mock data below)","Problem it targets: about 35% of rejected profiles were rejected for reasons the client had already stated in their preferences. Those rejections cost the client's trust and the matchmaker's time, and they drag acceptance down (31% overall, 21% for Matchmaker B)."],"features":["Pre-share preference check. Before a matchmaker emails a profile, every candidate is checked against the client's stated preferences and deal-breakers (age, height, religion, city/relocation, diet, marital status,…","ready to send: no misses, ranked by soft fit (profession, income, shared interests, closeness to the preferred age)","near misses: exactly one non-deal-breaker preference missed (\"age 37, client said 28-36\"). Clients do accept some of these, so the matchmaker checks with the client instead of the tool hard-blocking them","filtered out: a deal-breaker (smoking, drinking, children, relocation) or several misses","Rejection feedback structuring. Free-text rejection feedback is turned into structured reasons, and each rejection is labell